ity’s website and asking visitors to respond.\n2. Randomly selecting residents from the city census database and contacting them to ask about their commute times.\n3. Asking for responses from people who call into a local radio show about traffic."}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Unbiased Sampling Methods" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050431 :topic/math-academy-id 5982 :topic/title "Sampling Bias and Validity"}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186208757 :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186209398 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The sampling method is flawed and may produce a biased estimate of the mean number of books owned per household in the town." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186207708} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The survey proves that most families in the town own $85$ books." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186207709} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The sampling method is not flawed and is likely to produce an unbiased estimate of the mean number of owned books per household in the town." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186207710} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A determination about the mean number of books per household in the town should not be made because the sample size is too small." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186207711} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The mean number of books per household in the town is $85$." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186207712}] :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186207707}] :question/math-academy-id "q-306505" :question/problem "To estimate the average number of books owned per household in a town, Marcus surveyed $25$ families who were visiting the public library. For these $25$ families, the mean number of books per household was $85$. Which of the following statements **must**